Fix OpenCL C++ bindings build with libc++ in C++20 mode (macOS)

The bundled OpenCL-CLHPP cl2.hpp (2.0.10) declares
  using BuildLogType = vector<std::pair<cl::Device, ...>>;
and the BuildError class that uses it before cl::Device is complete.
libc++'s C++20 std::pair constructor checks need complete types, so this
fails with "no matching constructor for initialization of std::pair".
Move that block after the Device class, as upstream did in
https://github.com/KhronosGroup/OpenCL-CLHPP/pull/175 (issue #167).

Also add the bundled headers to the include path: CMake only adds
OpenCL_INCLUDE_DIRS for the tests, so the fallback to
external/opencl-clhpp (used when no system CLHPP is found) was never
reachable from src/core.

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index 0e4ac86..b8ce5fe 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -102,6 +102,7 @@ if (USE_OPENCL)
             message(STATUS "Couldn't find OpenCL C++ headers, using internal: ${OPENCL_HPP_INCLUDE_DIR}")
         endif()
         set(OpenCL_INCLUDE_DIRS ${OpenCL_INCLUDE_DIRS} ${OPENCL_HPP_INCLUDE_DIR})
+        include_directories(SYSTEM ${OPENCL_HPP_INCLUDE_DIR})
     else()
         message(STATUS "Couldn't find OpenCL: support DISABLED")
     endif()
